Controlling the trade-off between factuality and coverage using β. Figure [3](#page-8-1) illustrates how different values of β affect the trade-off between factuality and coverage scores. Users can adjust β based on their evaluation priorities: values of β < 1 give more weight to factuality score, while β > 1 emphasizes on coverage. In our experiments, for lower β values, GPT-4 and Mixtral demonstrate superior performance in terms of ICATβ. However, as β increases and coverage becomes more important, GPT-4 and Llama achieve higher scores due to their stronger Coverage Score.

